<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Rmangal on KevCaz's Website</title><link>https://kevcaz.github.io/tags/rmangal/</link><description>Recent content in Rmangal on KevCaz's Website</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><copyright>Content under CC0 1.0 Universal unless otherwise specified.</copyright><lastBuildDate>Sat, 07 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://kevcaz.github.io/tags/rmangal/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>rmangal is back on the CRAN</title><link>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2026/02/2024-02-07-rmangal-2-2-2/</link><pubDate>Sat, 07 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2026/02/2024-02-07-rmangal-2-2-2/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;At last, after substantial efforts, &lt;a href="https://docs.ropensci.org/rmangal/"&gt;rmangal&lt;/a&gt; made it back to the &lt;a href="https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/rmangal/index.html"&gt;CRAN&lt;/a&gt; on January 21, 2026. Below, I gathered a few notes about this important update.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="rmangal-was-archived"&gt;&lt;code&gt;rmangal&lt;/code&gt; was archived&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In March 2024, &lt;code&gt;rmangal&lt;/code&gt; was archived. A few days before, I received this message from the CRAN team:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dear maintainer,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please see the problems shown on &lt;a href="https://cran.r-project.org/web/checks/check_results_rmangal.html"&gt;https://cran.r-project.org/web/checks/check_results_rmangal.html&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please correct before 2024-03-01 to safely retain your package on CRAN.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It seems we need to remind you of the CRAN policy:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>rmangal 2.1.2</title><link>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2023/01/2023-01-31_rmangal_2_1/</link><pubDate>Tue, 31 Jan 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2023/01/2023-01-31_rmangal_2_1/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A new release of rmangal is now &lt;a href="https://CRAN.R-project.org/package=rmangal"&gt;available on CRAN&lt;/a&gt;. Following up on a recent issue in vcr (see &lt;a href="https://github.com/ropensci/vcr/issues/255"&gt;'
Overview of fixes for upcoming v1.2&amp;rsquo;&lt;/a&gt; for more details), I decided to have fixtures written in JSON rather than in YAML, the change was pretty straightforward&lt;/p&gt;
